WEBVTT

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:03.075
[MAYA] And now, I shall
hereby hand down my verdict!

00:00:03.158 --> 00:00:05.658
I find the defendant,
super guilty!

00:00:05.741 --> 00:00:08.575
No! If only I had
an Ace Attorney to help!

00:00:08.658 --> 00:00:10.241
[PHOENIX]
Objection!

00:00:10.325 --> 00:00:11.741
[MAYA]
Who is that?

00:00:11.825 --> 00:00:13.616
[PHOENIX] A man who
believes in his clients.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:15.866
And will strike down
any evildoers!

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:20.408
Lawyer Samurai,
Phoenix Wright enters the fray!

00:00:20.491 --> 00:00:22.158
Sally Forth!

00:00:22.241 --> 00:00:24.075
Going to court, you say?

00:00:24.158 --> 00:00:26.408
Call Wright and
company right away!

00:00:29.283 --> 00:00:31.450
[PHOENIX groans]

00:00:31.533 --> 00:00:33.116
[MAYA]
Hmm. Nope.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.575
One more time!
With some feeling!

00:00:35.658 --> 00:00:37.491
[groans]
Do we have to?

00:00:37.575 --> 00:00:38.741
You bet!

00:00:38.825 --> 00:00:40.366
We're not stopping until
we get the perfect take.

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:41.866
--[stomach growling]
--[BOTH gasp]

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:44.158
[MAYA]
Well, maybe after a snack.

00:00:44.241 --> 00:00:46.366
[PHOENIX]
I'm not cut out for showbiz.

00:02:18.616 --> 00:02:20.866
Huh? You're really
gonna stop filming?

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:24.408
[coughs] I think we should
try exploring other avenues

00:02:24.491 --> 00:02:25.616
to get the word out.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:27.200
I get ya.

00:02:27.283 --> 00:02:29.283
You just don't feel like the
Lawyer Samurai character works.

00:02:29.366 --> 00:02:31.908
--Well...
--How's this for an idea?

00:02:31.991 --> 00:02:34.116
A new character, called
the Lawyer General.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:35.950
You're completely
missing the issue here.

00:02:36.033 --> 00:02:37.700
[ <i>Signal Samurai</i> theme plays]

00:02:37.783 --> 00:02:39.200
[gasps]
It's your song!

00:02:39.283 --> 00:02:41.116
The <i>Signal Samurai</i> theme!

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.033
Reminds me of when I was a kid.

00:02:43.116 --> 00:02:45.783
That was your favorite right?
You still have the figures.

00:02:45.866 --> 00:02:48.241
Radio, huh?

00:02:48.325 --> 00:02:50.325
[MAYA]
Hmm? What's on your mind?

00:02:50.408 --> 00:02:53.325
Oh. I just kind of
have a thing for radio.

00:02:53.408 --> 00:02:56.075
[MAYA] Really? I bet
there's a story behind that!

00:02:56.158 --> 00:02:57.200
[PHOENIX]
Hmm.

00:02:59.033 --> 00:03:02.283
[PHOENIX] Well, it all started
when I was in middle school.

00:03:02.366 --> 00:03:04.450
[PHOENIX hums]

00:03:05.783 --> 00:03:07.075
[BUTZ]
Yo!

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:10.991
Hey, man.

00:03:11.075 --> 00:03:12.575
Hey, Nick.

00:03:12.658 --> 00:03:15.575
So, did you watch
<i>Rainbow Samurai</i> yesterday?

00:03:15.658 --> 00:03:16.658
[BUTZ]
Huh?

00:03:16.741 --> 00:03:18.575
Take down evil
with colorful justice!

00:03:18.658 --> 00:03:21.491
No way. I told ya,
I grew out of that kid's stuff

00:03:21.575 --> 00:03:23.491
after Signal Samurai.

00:03:23.575 --> 00:03:25.866
What a buzzkill.

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:27.533
Yeah, yeah whatever.

00:03:27.616 --> 00:03:30.533
Radio's my jam.
Grown-ups only.

00:03:30.616 --> 00:03:32.658
You don't say.

00:03:32.741 --> 00:03:34.825
[DEE] Sending you some good
vibes while you grab some

00:03:34.908 --> 00:03:38.116
quick bites, it's your portable
lunch date, Delicious Dee.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:40.950
She's sweet and yummy.

00:03:41.033 --> 00:03:42.950
[DEE] Watch out for this
track 'cause it's spicy!

00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:45.825
Hold the wasabi and taste
the fire through the airways.

00:03:45.908 --> 00:03:47.200
Aw, yeah!

00:03:47.283 --> 00:03:49.700
So, this is you
being an adult, huh?

00:03:51.366 --> 00:03:54.950
[BUTZ]
Hm? You dropped something, bro.

00:03:55.033 --> 00:03:56.533
[PHOENIX gasps ]

00:03:56.616 --> 00:03:59.325
I can't believe you still carry
that dinky little thing around.

00:03:59.408 --> 00:04:00.575
Yeah, well...

00:04:00.658 --> 00:04:02.491
I'd bet my life ol'
Edgy-boy's thrown his

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:04.366
in the trash by now.

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:08.991
Sounds like something he'd do.

00:04:09.075 --> 00:04:10.783
After all, he transferred
without telling us

00:04:10.866 --> 00:04:12.033
how to keep in contact.

00:04:12.116 --> 00:04:14.366
I don't think it's fair
to blame him for that!

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:16.325
When you think about
what happened to him.

00:04:16.408 --> 00:04:18.700
Yeah, you're
not wrong, but still.

00:04:18.783 --> 00:04:20.075
[PHOENIX]
Three years ago.

00:04:20.158 --> 00:04:22.033
There was a horrible murder
that actually happened

00:04:22.116 --> 00:04:24.200
inside the courthouse!

00:04:24.283 --> 00:04:28.450
The victim was Miles' father.
A prominent defense attorney.

00:04:28.533 --> 00:04:30.408
With nobody left to call family,

00:04:30.491 --> 00:04:32.908
Miles had to move out of town.

00:04:32.991 --> 00:04:36.658
We haven't heard so much
as a word from him since.

00:04:36.741 --> 00:04:38.866
We still don't know
who killed his dad.

00:04:38.950 --> 00:04:42.866
But whoever it was
left him to die alone.

00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:45.658
[PHOENIX] Wherever Miles is,
I hope he's okay.

00:04:45.741 --> 00:04:47.200
[BUTZ]
Yeah me, too.

00:04:47.283 --> 00:04:49.325
And I hope his li'l
pup is doing well.

00:04:55.908 --> 00:05:00.283
[MISSILE yipping]

00:05:05.825 --> 00:05:07.200
[MISSILE pants]

00:05:07.283 --> 00:05:08.408
[MILES]
Uh...

00:05:08.491 --> 00:05:09.491
[MISSILE barks]

00:05:09.575 --> 00:05:12.075
Cool. Right? He looks like Papa.

00:05:12.158 --> 00:05:13.866
Why'd you go and dress him up?

00:05:14.783 --> 00:05:16.075
Well, because...

00:05:16.158 --> 00:05:17.658
...I thought it would
make you smile.

00:05:17.741 --> 00:05:19.116
[gasps]

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:21.991
[gasps] I think this cravat
suits him better, though.

00:05:22.075 --> 00:05:24.450
[MISSILE whines]

00:05:24.533 --> 00:05:26.783
[FRANZISKA]
Hey! Don't go! Come back!

00:05:26.866 --> 00:05:27.950
[sighs]

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:36.658
[pants, barks]

00:05:36.741 --> 00:05:37.825
[FRANZISKA yelps]

00:05:37.908 --> 00:05:39.741
[NARRATOR]
Yo, yo, yo!

00:05:39.825 --> 00:05:42.533
Seven blades of justice,
each a different shade!

00:05:42.616 --> 00:05:46.116
[RAINBOW SAMURAI]
We are the Rainbow Samurai!

00:05:48.866 --> 00:05:50.075
[FRANZISKA]
That's so lame.

00:05:52.033 --> 00:05:53.741
[MISSILE pants]

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:01.200
[KARMA]
Hm?

00:06:04.658 --> 00:06:07.116
I'm glad you're home, Papa.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.741
[MILES]
Welcome back, sir.

00:06:08.825 --> 00:06:09.825
[KARMA]
Hm.

00:06:17.325 --> 00:06:18.491
How was court today?

00:06:18.575 --> 00:06:21.033
I'm sure you won,
like you always do, right?

00:06:21.116 --> 00:06:22.283
But of course.

00:06:22.366 --> 00:06:23.866
That's because you're the best!

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:28.033
Some day, I'm going to be
a prosecutor, like you.

00:06:28.116 --> 00:06:29.575
Obviously.

00:06:29.658 --> 00:06:31.741
Will you follow in your
father's footsteps?

00:06:31.825 --> 00:06:35.366
[MILES gasps]
Oh. I'm not quite sure.

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:36.991
I know.

00:06:37.075 --> 00:06:39.866
Why don't you take Miles to one
of your trials sometime, Papa?

00:06:39.950 --> 00:06:41.825
Oh. He doesn't have to.

00:06:41.908 --> 00:06:43.366
Consider it done.

00:06:43.450 --> 00:06:44.950
[FRANZISKA]
Yay! In that case,

00:06:45.033 --> 00:06:46.283
I'd like to go with you--

00:06:46.366 --> 00:06:48.283
there's something I really
want to do afterwards!

00:07:00.825 --> 00:07:02.116
[MILES]
I miss you...

00:07:03.533 --> 00:07:05.658
[KARMA] Let's get to work
on this orphanage deal.

00:07:05.741 --> 00:07:07.741
I'll be sending
Miles there soon.

00:07:09.366 --> 00:07:13.491
[groans]
That damned old wound.

00:07:13.575 --> 00:07:16.116
You're still trying to get in
my way, aren't you, Edgeworth?

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:17.991
Even beyond the grave.

00:07:27.366 --> 00:07:30.033
Let him go!
Don't hurt my father!

00:07:30.866 --> 00:07:31.783
[gunshot]

00:07:31.866 --> 00:07:33.783
[KARMA bellows]

00:07:36.116 --> 00:07:37.533
[gasps]

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:42.241
[MISSILE whines]

00:07:47.033 --> 00:07:48.741
[DEE]
So what's on today's lunch menu?

00:07:48.825 --> 00:07:50.325
I'm being bad and
having jelly donuts.

00:07:50.408 --> 00:07:51.658
Yum, yum, yum, yum.

00:07:51.741 --> 00:07:53.783
Yum-my!

00:07:56.491 --> 00:07:58.325
[PHOENIX]
Cutting class, I see.

00:07:59.283 --> 00:08:02.783
[DEE] All right, my Dee-vo-tees,
this one is a special request!

00:08:02.866 --> 00:08:05.825
[PHOENIX]
Yes! That's it!

00:08:05.908 --> 00:08:08.033
This is how we can
get in touch with Miles!

00:08:08.116 --> 00:08:09.366
Huh?

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:11.033
[PHOENIX chuckles]

00:08:11.116 --> 00:08:13.450
[LAWYER growls]
This wasn't in discovery.

00:08:13.533 --> 00:08:15.158
I object!

00:08:15.241 --> 00:08:16.866
[KARMA] It's your fault
for not being thorough

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:18.325
in your investigation.

00:08:18.408 --> 00:08:21.075
Von Karma is
meticulousness personified.

00:08:21.158 --> 00:08:23.200
But you are a subpar attorney.

00:08:23.283 --> 00:08:26.533
Don't forget: Someone's
life is in your hands.

00:08:28.825 --> 00:08:30.408
Guilty!

00:08:30.491 --> 00:08:32.491
[CROWD cheering]

00:08:32.575 --> 00:08:34.158
[gasps]

00:08:34.241 --> 00:08:36.658
[EDGEWORTH] Von Karma's
an extraordinary attorney.

00:08:36.741 --> 00:08:39.200
But, aren't prosecutors
your enemies?

00:08:39.283 --> 00:08:41.533
That's not how I look at it.

00:08:41.616 --> 00:08:44.408
We fight each other, sure,
but to find the truth.

00:08:44.491 --> 00:08:46.741
At the end of the day, it's
both our jobs to make sure

00:08:46.825 --> 00:08:48.908
evil is punished.

00:08:48.991 --> 00:08:51.366
Or at least, that's
how it should be.

00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:59.241
Incredible work.
Would you like to comment?

00:08:59.325 --> 00:09:01.575
[REPORTER B] Your perfect
record remains intact!

00:09:01.658 --> 00:09:03.825
I don't care about my record.

00:09:03.908 --> 00:09:07.116
I fight for justice.
That's my duty.

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:09.116
[FRANZISKA] Papa never
lets any criminals get away.

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:10.783
He always wins!

00:09:10.866 --> 00:09:13.366
He's basically a superhero.

00:09:13.450 --> 00:09:15.950
I can't wait to grow up
and be just like him.

00:09:16.033 --> 00:09:17.991
Maybe I'll even get
to be his partner.

00:09:19.991 --> 00:09:22.450
[FRANZISKA]
Papa!

00:09:22.533 --> 00:09:24.741
Your case was
absolutely perfect.

00:09:24.825 --> 00:09:26.158
[KARMA]
Naturally.

00:09:26.241 --> 00:09:27.825
Brilliant cross-examining.

00:09:27.908 --> 00:09:30.325
If only your father
had been my opponent.

00:09:30.408 --> 00:09:32.700
Then I might actually
have enjoyed myself.

00:09:32.783 --> 00:09:34.950
[gasps]

00:09:35.033 --> 00:09:37.950
Why don't the
two of you wait in the car.

00:09:38.033 --> 00:09:39.241
'Kay!

00:09:46.325 --> 00:09:48.700
[FRANZISKA gasps]

00:09:48.783 --> 00:09:50.075
[MISSILE barks]

00:09:50.158 --> 00:09:51.825
Can you spare some
change for these dogs?

00:09:51.908 --> 00:09:53.783
A little goes a long way!

00:09:55.241 --> 00:09:57.200
Hey, come on! Let's shop.

00:09:57.283 --> 00:09:58.575
[MILES]
Sure.

00:10:01.616 --> 00:10:03.866
[FRANZISKA] I think this
place is huge overseas.

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:05.825
But there's only one in Japan.

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:09.408
Whaddaya think?
The red one or the blue one?

00:10:09.491 --> 00:10:11.283
Uh. I dunno.

00:10:11.366 --> 00:10:13.116
Well. In that case...

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:14.658
...I'll go with the red one.

00:10:14.741 --> 00:10:17.950
It's almost the same
color as your vest!

00:10:18.033 --> 00:10:20.658
Oh! Papa! Look at these!

00:10:20.741 --> 00:10:22.450
[MISSILE barks]

00:10:22.533 --> 00:10:24.950
[FRANZISKA gasps]
Wait! Come back!

00:10:25.033 --> 00:10:26.908
Stay here. I'll go get him.

00:10:26.991 --> 00:10:28.700
Sure. Please hurry!

00:10:32.908 --> 00:10:34.700
Missile! C'mere!

00:10:37.283 --> 00:10:38.533
[gasps]

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:41.325
Please, forgive me.

00:10:44.491 --> 00:10:46.866
[GOLDY]
Hmph! What a rude boy.

00:10:54.825 --> 00:10:56.491
[DEE]
Now for some serious news.

00:10:56.575 --> 00:10:58.283
A little poor doggo's
gotten lost in

00:10:58.366 --> 00:11:00.533
the Lordly Tailor Shopping Mall.

00:11:00.616 --> 00:11:02.700
Lordly Tailor? Wait, here?

00:11:02.783 --> 00:11:05.241
[DEE] Her name is Napalm,
and she's a white Pomeranian

00:11:05.325 --> 00:11:07.075
wearing a cute
little pink ribbon.

00:11:07.158 --> 00:11:10.200
The heart-shaped spot on her
belly makes her extra special!

00:11:10.283 --> 00:11:12.700
The owner's really
worried about her.

00:11:12.783 --> 00:11:16.283
Wait, is this right?
There's a 5,000 dollar reward?

00:11:17.575 --> 00:11:20.491
I guess my dog's not the
only troublemaker here today.

00:11:20.575 --> 00:11:22.658
[DEE] Anyway,
here's a special request.

00:11:22.741 --> 00:11:26.158
[Signal Samurai theme plays

00:11:26.241 --> 00:11:28.033
Signal Samurai?

00:11:28.116 --> 00:11:33.366
[theme continues to play]

00:11:33.450 --> 00:11:34.783
You guys...

00:11:34.866 --> 00:11:38.116
I want to become a defense
lawyer, just like my dad.

00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:40.658
[gasps]
You'd be amazing!

00:11:40.741 --> 00:11:43.741
I can't wait to watch
you battle in court!

00:11:43.825 --> 00:11:45.033
[gasps]

00:11:47.533 --> 00:11:49.950
I can't wait to grow up
and be just like him.

00:11:50.033 --> 00:11:51.950
Maybe I'll even get
to be his partner.

00:11:53.741 --> 00:11:56.075
If only your father
had been my opponent.

00:11:56.158 --> 00:11:58.491
Then I might actually
have enjoyed myself.

00:12:01.033 --> 00:12:03.575
[MILES]
Father. What should I do?

00:12:05.366 --> 00:12:06.825
[DEE]
What a catchy throwback.

00:12:06.908 --> 00:12:09.700
That's a request coming
to you from Signal Blue.

00:12:09.783 --> 00:12:10.741
[MILES gasps]

00:12:10.825 --> 00:12:12.158
[DEE]
Oh, wow, cool!

00:12:12.241 --> 00:12:14.491
It even comes with
a heartfelt message.

00:12:14.575 --> 00:12:16.783
Signal Red.
Hope you're doin' well.

00:12:16.866 --> 00:12:18.450
We miss you.

00:12:18.533 --> 00:12:19.908
[DEE, PHOENIX]
And your puppy, too.

00:12:19.991 --> 00:12:21.533
[PHOENIX] I really wish
we were all together

00:12:21.616 --> 00:12:23.991
playing Signal Samurai again.

00:12:24.075 --> 00:12:26.033
I know you had to
move away suddenly,

00:12:26.116 --> 00:12:28.033
but know it doesn't
matter where you live.

00:12:28.116 --> 00:12:30.950
I've always got your back
and am rooting for you.

00:12:31.033 --> 00:12:32.491
We'll meet again one day.

00:12:32.575 --> 00:12:34.783
I know it.

00:12:34.866 --> 00:12:36.450
That was you, Wright?

00:12:36.533 --> 00:12:38.908
[DEE] I hope Red and
Blue meet again, too!

00:12:38.991 --> 00:12:41.158
Darlin' Dee's
cheering for you two!

00:12:41.241 --> 00:12:42.783
You never change, do you?

00:12:42.866 --> 00:12:43.991
I'm glad.

00:12:44.075 --> 00:12:46.200
[MISSILE barks]

00:12:46.283 --> 00:12:47.325
[MILES gasps]

00:12:48.283 --> 00:12:52.075
[NAPALM whines]

00:12:52.158 --> 00:12:54.616
I see. So that's
why you ran away.

00:12:56.741 --> 00:12:59.241
[MILES] A white Pomeranian
wearing a ribbon.

00:13:00.783 --> 00:13:03.366
You must be Napalm, right?

00:13:03.450 --> 00:13:06.866
[GOLDY]
Ah. There's my widdle baby.

00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:08.158
[MILES gasps]

00:13:08.241 --> 00:13:10.200
I looked all over for you.

00:13:10.283 --> 00:13:12.325
You naughty little pup.

00:13:18.325 --> 00:13:19.408
[FRANZISKA sighs]

00:13:20.991 --> 00:13:22.241
What's wrong?

00:13:22.325 --> 00:13:25.575
We came all the way here
so you could eat pancakes.

00:13:25.658 --> 00:13:26.700
I know.

00:13:29.908 --> 00:13:32.991
But... I want to wait for Miles.

00:13:33.075 --> 00:13:36.325
Thank you so much
for finding my precious girl.

00:13:36.408 --> 00:13:39.991
I'm Goldy. And that fluffy
nugget is my bad dog.

00:13:40.075 --> 00:13:42.075
Ah. You're the owner?

00:13:42.158 --> 00:13:43.283
Thank goodness.

00:13:43.366 --> 00:13:46.450
Oh, yes. I was
so worried about her.

00:13:46.533 --> 00:13:48.741
[NAPALM growls]

00:13:48.825 --> 00:13:50.283
Oh, she's playing.

00:13:50.366 --> 00:13:53.366
She's mad that her mama lost
track of her while shopping.

00:13:53.450 --> 00:13:55.116
[MILES]
Yeah. Seems like it.

00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:56.533
I never did have kids.

00:13:56.616 --> 00:14:00.658
So. You know, I may have
spoiled her because of that.

00:14:00.741 --> 00:14:04.033
--[NAPALM growls]
--It's okay. Come to Mommy.

00:14:04.116 --> 00:14:05.991
Get over here!

00:14:06.075 --> 00:14:08.408
Poor dear. She's rattled.

00:14:08.491 --> 00:14:10.825
I guess I'll have to give
her some extra treats.

00:14:10.908 --> 00:14:12.658
[laughs]

00:14:12.741 --> 00:14:14.616
We're leaving, Napalm.

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:15.908
[NAPALM barks]

00:14:15.991 --> 00:14:17.450
It doesn't sound
like she's happy

00:14:17.533 --> 00:14:18.658
to be going with you.

00:14:18.741 --> 00:14:20.075
Is that right?

00:14:20.158 --> 00:14:22.491
So, you think you know
better than her mother, then.

00:14:22.575 --> 00:14:24.408
I don't mean
to sound rude, ma'am.

00:14:24.491 --> 00:14:27.075
But are you certain that
you're the owner of this dog?

00:14:27.158 --> 00:14:29.033
Why would I lie about that?

00:14:29.116 --> 00:14:30.450
[MILES]
I'm sorry.

00:14:30.533 --> 00:14:32.908
But something about this
situation is making me uneasy.

00:14:32.991 --> 00:14:35.991
I see. You're trying
to steal my dog?

00:14:36.075 --> 00:14:38.741
I knew you looked
like a delinquent.

00:14:38.825 --> 00:14:40.033
[MILES]
What was that?

00:14:40.116 --> 00:14:41.241
[FRANZISKA gasps]

00:14:43.158 --> 00:14:44.158
Miles--

00:14:47.116 --> 00:14:48.658
Here's a bit of advice.

00:14:48.741 --> 00:14:50.366
You've got an ugly mutt already.

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:53.200
If you know what's good for you,
you'll take him and leave now.

00:14:53.283 --> 00:14:54.283
[MISSILE barks]

00:14:54.366 --> 00:14:55.450
Do you have proof
that she's yours?

00:14:55.533 --> 00:14:57.783
[laughs]
Proof. Sure.

00:14:57.866 --> 00:14:59.908
I know everything
about my darling.

00:14:59.991 --> 00:15:00.908
[gasps]

00:15:00.991 --> 00:15:02.325
She loves being brushed.

00:15:02.408 --> 00:15:05.366
Especially on her tummy.
Isn't that right, sweetheart?

00:15:05.450 --> 00:15:08.200
She's got this adorable
heart-shaped spot on her belly

00:15:08.283 --> 00:15:10.741
that she likes tickled at
the end of the day.

00:15:10.825 --> 00:15:12.283
Ooh! Look, Look!

00:15:12.366 --> 00:15:13.991
[NAPALM whines]

00:15:14.075 --> 00:15:15.366
It's our favorite game!

00:15:15.450 --> 00:15:18.825
We play it every night
'cause she's my dog.

00:15:19.991 --> 00:15:24.033
Now. If we're done here,
I'd like to be on my way.

00:15:27.741 --> 00:15:29.241
[MILES]
Okay. Fine.

00:15:29.325 --> 00:15:34.991
[laughs] Come on, pumpkin.
We should get you home.

00:15:35.075 --> 00:15:36.533
[MISSILE whimpers]

00:15:36.616 --> 00:15:38.533
[NAPALM whines]

00:15:41.908 --> 00:15:45.533
[GOLDY] Stupid kid. Now that
reward money is all mine.

00:15:45.616 --> 00:15:49.033
[GOLDY singing Signal Samurai]
♪ O-O-Oh. Olde Tokyo. ♪

00:15:49.116 --> 00:15:50.533
Hold it!

00:15:50.616 --> 00:15:51.908
[gasps]

00:15:51.991 --> 00:15:54.616
One more thing.
That theme song...

00:15:54.700 --> 00:15:55.866
Are you a fan?

00:15:55.950 --> 00:15:57.783
I'm sorry, what do you mean?

00:15:57.866 --> 00:16:00.075
[MILES] Do you know
the TV show it's from?

00:16:00.158 --> 00:16:03.325
Um, maybe. It just happened
to pop into my head.

00:16:05.366 --> 00:16:06.408
[MILES]
Actually, there's something

00:16:06.491 --> 00:16:07.991
I've heard said before.

00:16:08.075 --> 00:16:10.033
That there are no such
things as coincidences

00:16:10.116 --> 00:16:11.658
or random occurrences.

00:16:11.741 --> 00:16:13.950
[GOLDY]
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:16:14.033 --> 00:16:16.366
Our actions are never
completely random.

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:18.866
Everything we do,
we do for a reason.

00:16:18.950 --> 00:16:21.491
It's almost the same
color as your vest!

00:16:21.575 --> 00:16:23.991
For example, the song
you were singing.

00:16:24.075 --> 00:16:26.366
You may think it came to
your mind out of nowhere.

00:16:26.450 --> 00:16:28.366
But I don't believe in chance.

00:16:29.700 --> 00:16:31.908
What I'm thinking is,
you heard it recently.

00:16:31.991 --> 00:16:33.033
[gasps]

00:16:33.116 --> 00:16:34.908
[DEE] Anyway, here's
a special request.

00:16:34.991 --> 00:16:37.408
[Signal Samurai theme plays]

00:16:37.491 --> 00:16:38.658
Just like me.

00:16:38.741 --> 00:16:40.866
You heard the song playing
a few minutes ago.

00:16:40.950 --> 00:16:42.283
--On the radio.
--[gasps]

00:16:42.366 --> 00:16:43.616
What's more...

00:16:43.700 --> 00:16:46.533
...at about the same time,
the DJ had some news.

00:16:46.616 --> 00:16:48.491
That whoever found this
poor lost dog would be

00:16:48.575 --> 00:16:50.325
rewarded handsomely.

00:16:50.408 --> 00:16:52.700
She even mentioned that
heart-shaped spot on her belly.

00:16:52.783 --> 00:16:54.991
Wait. I have no idea
what you're talking about.

00:16:55.075 --> 00:16:56.116
I heard nothing.

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:58.116
Then how'd the
song get in your head?

00:16:58.200 --> 00:17:00.366
Oh, I remember now.
Yeah, it was on TV earlier.

00:17:00.450 --> 00:17:03.075
It's the theme song
to a children's TV show.

00:17:03.158 --> 00:17:05.908
And before, you said
you didn't have any kids.

00:17:05.991 --> 00:17:07.950
Well. It's a popular
enough tune.

00:17:08.033 --> 00:17:09.158
I'm sure it was on in a store.

00:17:09.241 --> 00:17:10.783
[MILES]
Objection!

00:17:10.866 --> 00:17:12.366
[GOLDY gasps]

00:17:12.450 --> 00:17:16.283
I hate to break it you,
but that would be impossible.

00:17:16.366 --> 00:17:18.158
What? How come?

00:17:18.241 --> 00:17:20.366
[MILES]
Because... <i>Signal Samurai</i> ...

00:17:20.450 --> 00:17:22.658
...has been off the air
for three full years.

00:17:22.741 --> 00:17:25.033
[GOLDY wails]

00:17:25.116 --> 00:17:26.366
[NAPALM whines]

00:17:26.450 --> 00:17:27.741
Just admit it,

00:17:27.825 --> 00:17:30.825
you were listening to the
same station I was.

00:17:30.908 --> 00:17:33.033
Who the hell do you
think you are, brat?

00:17:33.116 --> 00:17:35.366
Don't you know not
to question your elders?

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:37.408
If you really are
the owner of that dog,

00:17:37.491 --> 00:17:39.200
aren't you forgetting something?

00:17:39.283 --> 00:17:41.366
Huh? What do you mean?

00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:43.241
Five thousand dollars.

00:17:43.325 --> 00:17:44.033
[gasps]

00:17:44.116 --> 00:17:45.991
I found Napalm for you.

00:17:46.075 --> 00:17:49.158
Which means...
you owe me a reward.

00:17:49.241 --> 00:17:51.408
[GOLDY growls]

00:17:51.491 --> 00:17:54.533
[MILES]
If you want to take her home.

00:17:54.616 --> 00:17:56.491
You'll have to pay me first.

00:17:56.575 --> 00:17:59.325
[GOLDY growls]

00:17:59.408 --> 00:18:02.116
[bellows]

00:18:04.116 --> 00:18:07.450
[GOLDY] You don't get to tell
a woman like me what to do.

00:18:07.533 --> 00:18:11.200
Hand over that
mutt and scram, kid!

00:18:11.283 --> 00:18:12.950
That's enough!

00:18:13.033 --> 00:18:13.991
[GOLDY]
Huh?!

00:18:14.075 --> 00:18:17.241
Your scheming
ends here. Be gone.

00:18:17.325 --> 00:18:19.158
Hey. Who are you?

00:18:19.241 --> 00:18:20.241
You can't just--

00:18:20.325 --> 00:18:22.533
[KARMA]
Oh. Can't I?

00:18:22.616 --> 00:18:25.450
Would you like to
present your case again?

00:18:25.533 --> 00:18:28.783
--In court, this time?
--[whip lashing]

00:18:28.866 --> 00:18:30.491
[FRANZISKA]
Hmph.

00:18:30.575 --> 00:18:34.825
[GOLDY whines]
No. I won't go back to prison!

00:18:34.908 --> 00:18:36.325
[sobs]

00:18:36.408 --> 00:18:40.741
[FRANZISKA] Miles. We've been
looking all over for you.

00:18:40.825 --> 00:18:42.866
I apologize for
causing you trouble.

00:18:45.825 --> 00:18:49.950
Let's go. I imagine the
pancakes must be ready by now.

00:18:50.033 --> 00:18:52.033
Yummy! Come on!

00:18:59.241 --> 00:19:01.991
[FRANZISKA sighs]
I had so much fun today.

00:19:02.075 --> 00:19:04.825
[VOLUNTEER] Please spare
some change for these pups!

00:19:04.908 --> 00:19:06.283
You can change a life!

00:19:06.991 --> 00:19:10.741
[MILES] Sir. If I receive
the reward money,

00:19:10.825 --> 00:19:13.158
can I donate it to
this animal shelter?

00:19:13.241 --> 00:19:14.283
Really?

00:19:14.366 --> 00:19:16.158
[VOLUNTEER]
Got some change to spare?

00:19:16.241 --> 00:19:18.491
--Save a dog!
--Please, sir.

00:19:20.658 --> 00:19:22.533
You're the one
who found the dog.

00:19:22.616 --> 00:19:24.783
Do as you wish.

00:19:24.866 --> 00:19:26.116
Thank you so much!

00:19:31.825 --> 00:19:33.741
[KARMA]
Regarding the orphanage.

00:19:33.825 --> 00:19:35.075
Let's table that.

00:19:38.283 --> 00:19:39.991
[KARMA] I've been wondering
what made me adopt

00:19:40.075 --> 00:19:41.991
that boy three years ago.

00:19:42.075 --> 00:19:45.283
When he was so hurt
over the loss of his father.

00:19:45.366 --> 00:19:48.366
And I think today,
I finally began to understand

00:19:48.450 --> 00:19:51.533
how we ended up
in this situation.

00:19:51.616 --> 00:19:53.658
It wasn't because of my guilt.

00:19:53.741 --> 00:19:57.325
I simply wanted to see where
the path of pain would lead us,

00:19:57.408 --> 00:19:59.408
and how he would
eventually develop.

00:19:59.491 --> 00:20:03.158
Karma has a strange
way of showing itself.

00:20:03.241 --> 00:20:05.658
You can wear this
from now on if you would like.

00:20:05.741 --> 00:20:06.741
[MILES gasps]

00:20:08.908 --> 00:20:10.991
[laughs]
Thanks!

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:25.658
Well, you helped
me out once again...

00:20:25.741 --> 00:20:26.866
...my friend.

00:20:31.533 --> 00:20:32.825
[gasps]

00:20:32.908 --> 00:20:35.533
[BUTZ] Huh? What are you
standing around for?

00:20:35.616 --> 00:20:36.616
Let's go.

00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:38.325
[PHOENIX]
Right! Coming.

00:22:10.783 --> 00:22:13.283
[MAYA] So? Did Edgeworth
really hear the song?

00:22:13.366 --> 00:22:14.700
How's it all end?

00:22:14.783 --> 00:22:15.700
Who knows?

00:22:15.783 --> 00:22:17.908
I'm sure it found
its way to him.

00:22:17.991 --> 00:22:19.616
Just like our killer
ad will reach him

00:22:19.700 --> 00:22:21.241
and everyone else in the world.

00:22:21.325 --> 00:22:22.825
Uh, yeah, about that...

00:22:22.908 --> 00:22:25.075
Now that it's done,
how do we get it out there?

00:22:25.158 --> 00:22:26.491
What are you talking about?

00:22:26.575 --> 00:22:28.158
We'll just throw it up on
the Internet and watch it

00:22:28.241 --> 00:22:29.616
rack up the likes. Easy!

00:22:29.700 --> 00:22:31.075
What are you waiting for?

00:22:31.158 --> 00:22:32.658
Upload it now.

00:22:32.741 --> 00:22:35.325
[PHOENIX] I don't know. I'm not
exactly great with computers.

00:22:35.408 --> 00:22:37.741
They're so... confusing.

00:22:37.825 --> 00:22:39.366
[MAYA hums]

00:22:40.908 --> 00:22:42.908
--Here goes.
--[gasps] Hold on!

00:22:42.991 --> 00:22:44.533
[MAYA]
And... done!

00:22:46.575 --> 00:22:47.908
[MAYA, PHOENIX] ♪ Call Wright
and company right away! ♪

00:22:47.991 --> 00:22:49.450
What the heck?

00:22:49.533 --> 00:22:52.658
Hey. You didn't tell us how
crazy Japanese law ads can be.

00:22:55.075 --> 00:22:56.200
[gasps]

00:23:09.616 --> 00:23:11.075
[sighs]

00:23:20.825 --> 00:23:22.366
[PHOENIX]
Objection!

00:23:22.450 --> 00:23:25.033
Maggey, The Goddess
of Misfortune, returns!

00:23:25.116 --> 00:23:28.616
And, just her luck, she's been
accused of murder yet again!

00:23:28.700 --> 00:23:31.741
This time, the crime happened
in a fancy French restaurant,

00:23:31.825 --> 00:23:34.366
and nobody believes
what she has to say.

00:23:34.450 --> 00:23:36.491
[PHOENIX] But even if
everyone thinks she's guilty,

00:23:36.575 --> 00:23:39.158
I'm on her side!
Trust me, Maggey!

00:23:39.241 --> 00:23:41.575
Find the contradictions!
Believe in the truth!

00:23:41.658 --> 00:23:44.575
Next episode: "Recipe for
Turnabout--1st Trial"!

00:23:44.658 --> 00:23:45.783
Take that!
